        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/runge-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A bandstand, originally built in the 1890s and rebuilt in 1924, has stood in Runge’s public square for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/runge-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The bandstand earned a historic marker in 1970, recognizing its long‑standing role in the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/runge-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1931, Runge erected a two‑story city hall, fire station, and auditorium that still serve the town today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/runge-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Runge’s climate features hot, humid summers and generally mild to cool winters, typical of central Texas.",
